### Job Attachment: list for an Enquiry, newest first.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v2/method/frappe.client.get_list
Authorization: token {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
	"doctype": "Job Attachment",
	"filters": [
		[ "enquiry", "=", "ENQ109" ]
	],
	"order_by": "creation desc",
	"fields": [
		"name",
		"creation",
		"enquiry",
		"date",
		"time",
		"employee",
		"employee.employee_name",
		"document",
		"is_photo"
	]
}



### Read Job Attachment by ID.

GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v2/document/Job Attachment/JOBATT1
Authorization: token {{token}}



### Create, step 1: upload the file.
	# Take "file_url" from the response for step 2: the server may rename the file, or reuse an identical one.
	# "is_private" = 1: only logged-in users who can read the Job Attachment can open the file.
	# Send no "doctype" / "docname": saving the Job Attachment in step 2 links the file to it.
	# The file is read from next to this .rest file.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v2/method/frappe.handler.upload_file
Authorization: token {{token}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=----LogicXBoundary

------LogicXBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="is_private"

1
------LogicXBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="IMG_20260923_131500.jpg"
Content-Type: image/jpeg

< ./IMG_20260923_131500.jpg
------LogicXBoundary--



### Create, step 2: the Job Attachment for the uploaded file.
	# "date" / "time" are optional: they default to the server's today / now.
	# "is_photo": 1 for a photo, 0 (the default) for a document.
	# A "Photo attached by ..." row, with a link to the file, is added to the Enquiry's Messages.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v2/document/Job Attachment
Authorization: token {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "enquiry": "ENQ109",
  "employee": "HR-EMP-00003",
  "document": "/private/files/IMG_20260923_131500.jpg",
  "is_photo": 1
}



### Open the file: {{baseUrl}} + "document". A private file needs the same Authorization header.
GET {{baseUrl}}/private/files/IMG_20260923_131500.jpg
Authorization: token {{token}}


